[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="ManualPage" load_steps=2 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/components/manual_page.gd" id="1_page"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_page")
title = "DAMAGE CONTROL"
body = "THE HULL is xenon-metal: a grown lattice, seamless and load-bearing. No weld, rivet or fastener exists anywhere on the primary structure, and no yard in service can manufacture or duplicate it. Repair what you can reach; do not cut into the frame.

MICRO-PUNCTURES are normal on a hull this age. Each one raises the compartment leak rate; pressure falls, and the leak keeps working while you sleep.

PATCH PROCEDURE
  1  CLEAN the breach
  2  FIT the patch
  3  APPLY SEALANT   (one cartridge per patch)
  4  VERIFY the seal
Verify against the panel's leak rate. A failed verify means a failed seal - do it again.

Take a sealant cartridge from the locker before you go; it must be in your hands at the seal step. The hull will not wait for a second trip."
